{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB 5% cap on Berkeley Annual General Adjustment","requirement":"The Annual General Adjustment, the yearly amount by which a landlord of a fully covered unit may raise rent, is capped at 5%; banked unused AGAs may still be used to raise rent to the rent ceiling.","key_value":"5% maximum AGA","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered units: most units in multifamily properties built before 1980, single-family homes with tenancies begun before 1996, rooms rented individually, and government-owned or -subsidized units newly covered by Measure BB.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1980","built_after":null,"date_basis":"unspecified","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Rent ceiling applies to fully covered units; partially covered units have no rent ceiling."},"exemptions":"Units with Section 202 or Section 811 subsidies, and Rent Supplement, Section 8 Loan Management Set Aside, and project-based Section 8 units in HUD-insured projects, are only partially covered; a unit where the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities is exempt only if the landlord lived on the same property at the tenancy's start.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":"Certain subsidized units are only partially covered because Federal law, State law, or administrative regulation prohibits rent control.","confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB changes to Berkeley just cause eviction grounds","requirement":"Landlords of covered units may evict only for just cause. Nonpayment eviction now requires debt of at least one month's Fair Market Rent; eviction for refusing to sign a similar lease is barred; lease-breach notices must describe the term and resulting harm.","key_value":"1 month's Fair Market Rent","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance, who may not be evicted without just cause; eviction notices and lawsuits must be filed with the Rent Board within three business days of service.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance."},"exemptions":"Units exempt from the Rent Ordinance, including a unit where the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities and the landlord lived on the same property at the tenancy's start.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
